WEBVTT

00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:03.176
Lolly turns your rules - colours, type,

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:06.264
layouts, logic - into tools anyone can use

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.977
to make finished files: images, PDF'S,

00:00:10.041 --> 00:00:12.684
social cards, video, by filling in a few

00:00:12.773 --> 00:00:13.944
fields.

00:00:14.716 --> 00:00:17.091
There's little to learn and nothing to

00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:20.370
upload: making and exporting runs on your

00:00:20.431 --> 00:00:22.969
device, online or off.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:27.550
This is the one page to read first.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:36.550
Two things get you productive: make Lolly yours and bring in what you already have «your design files and tokens».

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.550
Everything else is a link away.

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:43.796
New to Lolly and just want to make

00:00:43.859 --> 00:00:45.044
something?

00:00:45.807 --> 00:00:48.134
Open the app, pick any tool from the

00:00:48.196 --> 00:00:50.563
gallery, fill in the blanks, and hit

00:00:50.624 --> 00:00:51.719
Render.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.837
Come back here when you want it wearing

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:56.319
your brand.

00:00:57.463 --> 00:00:58.450
1.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:02.009
Make it yours - configure your Design

00:01:02.072 --> 00:01:03.052
System

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:06.228
Your brand in Lolly is a small

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:09.595
design-tokens document - colours, fonts,

00:01:09.654 --> 00:01:12.334
and a few rules - that every tool renders

00:01:12.394 --> 00:01:13.595
against.

00:01:14.372 --> 00:01:16.914
Set it once and everything you make is

00:01:16.987 --> 00:01:20.845
on-brand by construction, not by review.

00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:24.476
There are three ways in; pick the one that

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:27.819
matches where your brand already lives.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:32.950
Start from scratch «the design system builder»

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.475
First run drops you on the Start screen «#/start» - the Brand Studio.

00:01:39.825 --> 00:01:55.475
Give it a name and a primary colour and Lolly derives a complete, accessible palette from it - light/dark surfaces, text, accents - using the same colour maths the engine uses everywhere else.

00:01:55.825 --> 00:02:01.100
Pick a font, and you have a working brand in under a minute.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:14.350
From there the studio's five tabs «Logos, Colours, Type, Tokens, Catalogue» let you take it as far as you like - refine any of it later, whenever you come back.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:22.875
You can always revisit this from the dashboard «provided you arent using a brand-locked version of lolly»

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.950
Import a brand you already have

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:41.500
If your brand is already captured as design tokens - from Penpot, Tokens Studio «Figma», or any plain DTCG file - bring it in wholesale rather than retyping it.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.700
Two routes:

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:58.400
In the app: the design system builder: Brand Studio «#/start» accepts a token file, a Penpot export, or a LollyBrand pack directly - drop it in and the palette lights up.

00:02:59.143 --> 00:03:01.838
From the command line, to stand up a

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.969
reusable brand pack:

00:03:04.753 --> 00:03:07.617
Code example omitted.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:25.550
ingest:brand accepts all three containers Penpot / Tokens Studio export the same document in - a single tokens-json, a directory «$metadata-json + per-set files», or a project-penpot archive.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:34.275
With --activate it registers the brand as a profile, switches to it, and rebuilds the catalog.

00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:40.500
See Configuration for how brand packs and profiles fit together.

00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:43.782
Tune it in the app

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:57.100
Once a brand is active, keep shaping it in the Brand Studio «#/start» - change a colour or a role and every preview across the app updates as you type.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:06.750
«The dashboard's Design system tab at #/d shows the brand read-only; the Studio is where you edit it.»

00:04:07.476 --> 00:04:09.791
The same brand is summarised on the

00:04:09.851 --> 00:04:13.120
Profile → Your brand card.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.051
Fonts are real: pick from Google Fonts and

00:04:17.111 --> 00:04:20.168
Lolly stores the file on your device as a

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:23.407
brand asset, so your typography travels

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.962
offline and nothing is fetched at render

00:04:26.026 --> 00:04:27.145
time.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.546
When you're happy, export the brand as a

00:04:30.607 --> 00:04:33.442
LollyBrand pack - a single file a

00:04:33.513 --> 00:04:36.239
colleague can import to get the exact same

00:04:36.301 --> 00:04:38.745
palette, fonts, and rules.

00:04:39.503 --> 00:04:42.206
That's how a brand moves between people

00:04:42.292 --> 00:04:45.089
and machines without a server in the

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.120
middle.

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:50.319
Brand tokens round-trip both ways.

00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:54.301
Because Lolly's brand is DTCG tokens - the

00:04:54.392 --> 00:04:57.546
format Penpot reads and writes natively

00:04:57.618 --> 00:05:00.321
and Tokens Studio brings to Figma - the

00:05:00.381 --> 00:05:03.029
palette you design with and the palette

00:05:03.089 --> 00:05:06.233
Lolly enforces are one document, not two

00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:08.995
lists you keep in sync by hand.

00:05:09.798 --> 00:05:12.293
See Design Tokens.

00:05:13.427 --> 00:05:14.378
2.

00:05:15.186 --> 00:05:18.005
Bring in what you already have

00:05:19.055 --> 00:05:22.344
You don't start from a blank page.

00:05:23.142 --> 00:05:26.286
Lolly opens the design work and the open

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.844
formats you already own.

00:05:29.973 --> 00:05:32.864
Open-source design files

00:05:33.807 --> 00:05:36.225
Finished work in Figma, Penpot,

00:05:36.285 --> 00:05:39.960
Illustrator, InDesign, or any SVG app

00:05:40.018 --> 00:05:42.402
doesn't have to stay locked in the app you

00:05:42.462 --> 00:05:43.770
drew it in.

00:05:44.537 --> 00:05:48.343
Open Layout Studio, click Import a design,

00:05:48.404 --> 00:05:51.321
and the file opens as a living layout -

00:05:51.377 --> 00:05:53.519
not a flattened picture.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:57.820
Every layer becomes an editable box: text

00:05:57.864 --> 00:06:00.737
stays retypable, shapes stay shapes,

00:06:00.798 --> 00:06:03.751
images land in your library, and complex

00:06:03.812 --> 00:06:06.819
vector art is preserved faithfully.

00:06:07.568 --> 00:06:10.457
It arrives already conformed to your brand

00:06:10.525 --> 00:06:12.820
faces and colour rules.

00:06:13.587 --> 00:06:16.467
The whole import happens on your device -

00:06:16.523 --> 00:06:19.315
the file is parsed in your browser and

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.344
nothing is uploaded.

00:06:22.121 --> 00:06:24.752
Full details, and exactly what carries

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.069
over, are in Import a design.

00:06:28.849 --> 00:06:32.068
Got a PowerPoint deck instead?

00:06:32.861 --> 00:06:34.234
Drop the .

00:06:35.051 --> 00:06:38.716
pptx on Deck Builder to edit it slide by

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.149
slide, already snapped to your brand - or

00:06:42.212 --> 00:06:45.074
run Rebrand a Deck to get the same deck

00:06:45.135 --> 00:06:48.256
back re-themed, charts and animations

00:06:48.325 --> 00:06:49.594
intact.

00:06:50.731 --> 00:06:53.679
From a one-off to a template

00:06:54.641 --> 00:06:57.850
Here's the payoff: an imported layout is

00:06:57.915 --> 00:07:01.072
an ordinary Layout Studio session, so once

00:07:01.127 --> 00:07:04.769
you save it, it lives at a URL.

00:07:05.528 --> 00:07:08.454
Anyone with Lolly can open that URL,

00:07:08.516 --> 00:07:11.372
change the words, swap an image, and

00:07:11.432 --> 00:07:14.139
render their own version - no design app,

00:07:14.197 --> 00:07:16.670
and the locked parts stay locked.

00:07:17.451 --> 00:07:22.143
A once-off design becomes a reusable tool.

00:07:22.911 --> 00:07:25.645
That's the whole idea, reached without

00:07:25.706 --> 00:07:28.794
writing a line of configuration.

00:07:29.937 --> 00:07:33.190
Open data and open tools

00:07:34.139 --> 00:07:37.053
The community tool set is open source and

00:07:37.114 --> 00:07:40.778
brand-agnostic - QR codes, street maps,

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.736
filters, privacy utilities - and it

00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:46.309
renders against your brand the moment you

00:07:46.383 --> 00:07:47.945
activate it.

00:07:48.726 --> 00:07:52.221
Feed tools your own open data too: paste

00:07:52.262 --> 00:07:56.287
or drop a CSV or JSON table and a tool's

00:07:56.344 --> 00:07:59.002
repeating fields fill from it, one

00:07:59.095 --> 00:08:01.394
finished asset per row.

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.619
3.

00:08:04.429 --> 00:08:07.812
Make something, then share or automate it

00:08:08.757 --> 00:08:11.612
With a brand active and your material in

00:08:11.673 --> 00:08:15.844
hand, every tool produces a finished file:

00:08:16.615 --> 00:08:20.898
Render any tool to SVG, PDF, PNG,

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.513
JPG, WebP, video, and more - at true print

00:08:24.585 --> 00:08:26.988
sizes and physical units when you need

00:08:27.046 --> 00:08:27.945
them.

00:08:28.739 --> 00:08:31.619
See Exporting & formats.

00:08:32.423 --> 00:08:34.144
Share a link.

00:08:34.905 --> 00:08:38.623
Every tool state is a URL, so a finished

00:08:38.711 --> 00:08:40.612
asset is reproducible and

00:08:40.672 --> 00:08:43.309
parameter-addressable - commit the link,

00:08:43.375 --> 00:08:45.720
regenerate on demand.

00:08:46.501 --> 00:08:48.619
Do it in bulk.

00:08:49.389 --> 00:08:52.255
Drive a template from a spreadsheet in the

00:08:52.316 --> 00:08:56.044
batch grid: one finished asset per row.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.568
Automate it.

00:08:59.335 --> 00:09:02.246
The same render runs from the CLI and from

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:07.019
an AI agent - a URL is the API.

00:09:07.755 --> 00:09:11.719
"A URL is the API" is literal.

00:09:12.488 --> 00:09:15.858
The chart below was not drawn by anyone:

00:09:15.924 --> 00:09:18.919
its type, its heading and its whole data

00:09:18.981 --> 00:09:22.070
table were typed into the address bar, and

00:09:22.111 --> 00:09:24.667
the same link renders the same chart on

00:09:24.726 --> 00:09:26.245
any device.

00:09:27.382 --> 00:09:29.479
Where to go next

00:09:30.511 --> 00:09:32.883
Three pathways, depending on what you're

00:09:32.943 --> 00:09:34.495
here to do:

00:09:35.293 --> 00:09:38.668
Lolly for Creators - you make things.

00:09:39.434 --> 00:09:42.413
The advantages, and how to get the most

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.070
out of the app.

00:09:44.867 --> 00:09:47.684
Lolly for Builders - you author tools,

00:09:47.745 --> 00:09:50.044
integrate, and deploy.

00:09:50.832 --> 00:09:53.893
The technical documentation.

00:09:54.688 --> 00:09:57.466
Lolly for Operators - you're responsible

00:09:57.557 --> 00:10:01.200
for brand, security, and rollout across an

00:10:01.261 --> 00:10:02.994
organisation.
